# Env file template. Vite reads .env / .env.local / .env.production.local
# at build/dev time. Variables prefixed VITE_ get inlined into the bundle
# (accessible via `import.meta.env.VITE_*`); the rest are only visible in the
# node context (vite.config.ts, plugins).
#
# Local development: copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in
# your own values. On CI/Cloudflare Pages - set the same variables through the
# CF dashboard (Pages -> Settings -> Environment
# variables -> Production / Preview).
#
# Sentry DSN for crash-reporting (errors-only). Public (visible in the
# bundle), not a secret. Own value per environment (beta -> beta project DSN,
# prod -> prod project DSN). Semantics:
#  - variable NOT set (no line at all) -> the SDK is fully tree-shaken out of
#    the bundle (dynamic import @sentry/browser gets tree-shaken, no @sentry
#    chunk). This is the mode for self-host forks and dev - zero Sentry bytes.
#  - empty value (VITE_SENTRY_DSN=) -> crash-reporting is disabled at runtime,
#    but the lazy @sentry chunk still ends up in dist (just not loaded). To cut
#    it out entirely - remove the line completely, don't leave it empty.
#  - valid DSN -> crash-reporting is enabled by default (opt-OUT in Settings).
# Server-side is mandatory too: in the Sentry project enable "Prevent Storing
# of IP Addresses" (Settings -> Security & Privacy) - the client-side
# sendDefaultPii:false is necessary but not sufficient.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Sentry source map upload (build-time, WITHOUT the VITE_ prefix) ---
# Uploads hidden source maps to Sentry so crash stack traces read in the
# original TS, not minified code. Active only when ALL THREE variables are
# set; otherwise the build doesn't emit maps at all (SENTRY_UPLOAD in vite.config.ts).
# Maps are uploaded to Sentry and then deleted from dist - they never reach
# the prod bundle. These values are SECRET (unlike the public DSN above): node
# context only during the build, never inlined into the client bundle. Works
# from inside the CF Pages build (maps must come from the same build that gets
# deployed).
#  - SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN - a token with scope project:releases + org:read. Create it:
#    Sentry -> Settings -> Auth Tokens (Organization Tokens).
#  - SENTRY_ORG / SENTRY_PROJECT - org and project slugs.
# On CF Pages set in Production (and Preview, if beta maps are needed).
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
